Package: bayesrep
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Repulsive Ensembles via Ising Priors
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "Anthony", "Christidis",
      email = "anthony.christidis@stat.ubc.ca",
      role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
  )
Description: A scalable, exact Gibbs sampling framework for Bayesian Repulsive
    Ensembles (BRE). An Ising prior on the feature-allocation matrix pushes the
    members of an ensemble towards structurally diverse sub-models, reducing
    collinearity-induced variance in high-dimensional regression and
    classification. The repulsion strength is learned from the data rather than
    tuned, a Beta hyperprior on feature-specific inclusion probabilities allows
    universally predictive covariates to be shared across sub-models, and
    Polya-Gamma data augmentation extends the exact sampler to binary outcomes.
    Posterior summaries are invariant to relabelling of the ensemble members.
